      "markdown": "### 2. (18%) On FA and Regular Languages\n\nSay whether each of the following languages is regular or not regular? Prove your answers.\n\n $$ L_{1}=\\{w|w\\in\\{0,1\\}^{*} $$ \n\n $$ L_{2}=\\{w|w\\in\\{0,1\\}^{*} $$ \n\n### 3. (20%) On PDA and Context-Free Languages\n\nLet  $ L_3 = \\{wca^m b^n | w \\in \\{a, b\\}^*  $, where  $ w = w^R $, and  $ m, n \\in \\mathbb{N}, n \\leq m \\leq 2n\\} $.\n\n(a) Give a context-free grammar for the language  $ L_{3} $.\n\n $$ \\mathrm{PDA}\\;M=(K,\\Sigma,\\Gamma,\\Delta,s,F) $$ \n\n $$ L_{3} $$ \n\n(b) The PDA  $  M = (K, \\Sigma, \\Gamma, \\Delta, s, F)  $ is defined below:\n\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"imgs/img_in_image_box_605_2426_1946_3274.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" width=\"54%\" /></div>\n",
